### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### 19 - IDENTITY, ACCESS & WORKSPACE SHARING  (Branch P109)
###
### Covers the NEW identity/access surface introduced by P109:
###   - First-owner bootstrap claim  (com.amsha.onboarding.BootstrapResource)
###   - Identity / profiles / workspace membership
###   - Invitations, member removal, ownership transfer
###   - Personal API credential issue/revoke
###   - Workspace credential rotation
###
### These endpoints live UNDER the new auth filter (ApiKeyAuthFilter)
### and require an authenticated principal (API key OR web session
### cookie). In this deployment they are served under the /api/v1
### context path: /api/v1/identity, /api/v1/onboarding/bootstrap, etc.
### (Set baseUrl accordingly.)
###
### PREREQUISITES
###   1. Fresh serve mode on http://localhost:8080 (UNCLAIMED state).
###      Bootstrap claim MUTATES durable state — run once per DB.
###   2. The first-owner key is returned ONLY in the `AMSHA_API_KEY`
###      Set-Cookie (httpOnly + secure + SameSite=Strict, by design:
###      the raw key is intentionally NOT in the JSON body). Copy the
###      value and paste it into @ownerApiKey below.
###
###      # capture from a shell:
###      curl -s -i -X POST http://localhost:8080/onboarding/bootstrap/claim \
###        | grep -i 'set-cookie'
###
### ROLE MODEL (P109): OWNER > ADMIN > MEMBER. Only an ACTIVE member
### may call workspace-scoped endpoints; only OWNER/ADMIN may invite;
### only OWNER may invite OWNERs, transfer ownership, or rotate
### workspace credentials.
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# @baseUrl    = http://localhost:8080
# @validKey   = key-internal-cWevfEoRvstUv0PqGpf02LzDY5kPNaz1y9GSl0LZOwU=
# @ciKey      = key-ci-JV/qXAikcUoSCCUsqYxLvNjxW/N3KROQtawg3VRFrJs=
# @invalidKey = totally-wrong-key

# ── PASTE first-owner key from the bootstrap claim Set-Cookie here ──
# @ownerApiKey = sk-PASTE_RAW_KEY_FROM_SET_COOKIE

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A. FIRST-OWNER BOOTSTRAP CLAIM  (loopback-only, once per DB)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [A1] Bootstrap status on fresh DB → 200, status "UNCLAIMED"
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/onboarding/bootstrap/status

### [A2] Claim first owner → 200 {ownerId, workspaceId}
###      Sets cookie: AMSHA_API_KEY=<rawKey>; HttpOnly; Secure; SameSite=Strict
###      (rawKey is deliberately absent from the JSON body)
###      Loopback-only: a non-loopback caller would get 403 FORBIDDEN.
# @name bootstrapClaim
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/onboarding/bootstrap/claim

### [A3] Status after claim → 200, status CLAIMED or CREDENTIAL_ISSUED
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/onboarding/bootstrap/status

### [A4] Re-claim → 409 ALREADY_CLAIMED (idempotency guard)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/onboarding/bootstrap/claim

### [A5] Confirm claim → 200 {success:true}
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/onboarding/bootstrap/confirm
Content-Type: application/json

{ "expectedRevision": 1 }

### [A6] Confirm again → 400 INVALID_STATE (state already moved past CREDENTIAL_ISSUED)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/onboarding/bootstrap/confirm
Content-Type: application/json

{ "expectedRevision": 1 }

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# B. IDENTITY /me
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [B1] /identity/me with first-owner key → 200 {user, memberships[]}
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/identity/me
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{ownerApiKey}}

### [B2] /identity/me with NO key → 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/identity/me

### [B3] /identity/me with invalid key → 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/identity/me
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{invalidKey}}

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# C. WORKSPACE MEMBERS  (needs ownerKey; wsId from claim body)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [C1] List members of own workspace → 200 [ {role:"OWNER",...} ]
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/identity/workspaces/{{bootstrapClaim.response.body.workspaceId}}/members
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{ownerApiKey}}

### [C2] List members with NO key → 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/identity/workspaces/{{bootstrapClaim.response.body.workspaceId}}/members

### [C3] List members of unknown workspace → 403 (not an active member)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/identity/workspaces/ws_doesnotexist/members
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{ownerApiKey}}

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# D. INVITATIONS
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [D1] Owner creates a MEMBER invitation → 200 {invitationId, rawToken, expiresAt}
# @name invite
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/identity/workspaces/{{bootstrapClaim.response.body.workspaceId}}/invitations
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{ownerApiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "role": "MEMBER" }

### [D2] Owner creates an OWNER invitation → 200 (owner may grant OWNER)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/identity/workspaces/{{bootstrapClaim.response.body.workspaceId}}/invitations
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{ownerApiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "role": "OWNER" }

### [D3] Invalid role → 403 FORBIDDEN
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/identity/workspaces/{{bootstrapClaim.response.body.workspaceId}}/invitations
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{ownerApiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "role": "WIZARD" }

### [D4] Accept with bogus token → 404 INVITATION_NOT_FOUND
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/identity/invitations/bogus-token/accept
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{ownerApiKey}}

### [D5] Accept the real token (requires a SECOND registered user;
###      with only the first owner this re-adds owner as member).
###      In a single-owner DB this is a no-op success: 200.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/identity/invitations/{{invite.response.body.rawToken}}/accept
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{ownerApiKey}}

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# E. PERSONAL API CREDENTIALS
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [E1] Create credential with OWNER role (owner holds OWNER) → 200 {credentialId, rawKey, expiresAt}
# @name cred
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/identity/api-credentials
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{ownerApiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "roleSet": "OWNER", "expiresInSeconds": 3600 }

### [E2] Cannot grant INTERNAL role → 403 FORBIDDEN_ROLE
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/identity/api-credentials
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{ownerApiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "roleSet": "INTERNAL" }

### [E3] Cannot grant a role the caller does not hold (ADMIN) → 403 FORBIDDEN_ROLE
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/identity/api-credentials
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{ownerApiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "roleSet": "ADMIN" }

### [E4] Revoke the credential → 200 {success:true}
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/identity/api-credentials/{{cred.response.body.credentialId}}
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{ownerApiKey}}

### [E5] Revoke non-existent → 404
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/identity/api-credentials/cred_doesnotexist
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{ownerApiKey}}

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# F. MEMBER REMOVAL  (last-owner guard)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [F1] Remove a non-member → 404 (target not found)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/identity/workspaces/{{bootstrapClaim.response.body.workspaceId}}/members/usr_doesnotexist
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{ownerApiKey}}

### [F2] Remove the only OWNER → 400 LAST_OWNER_REMOVAL_BLOCKED
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/identity/workspaces/{{bootstrapClaim.response.body.workspaceId}}/members/{{bootstrapClaim.response.body.ownerId}}
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{ownerApiKey}}

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# G. OWNERSHIP TRANSFER  (needs a second ACTIVE member — negative here)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [G1] Transfer to a non-member → 400 TARGET_NOT_MEMBER
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/identity/workspaces/{{bootstrapClaim.response.body.workspaceId}}/owner/transfer
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{ownerApiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "targetUserId": "usr_doesnotexist" }

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# H. WORKSPACE CREDENTIAL ROTATION  (RUN LAST — revokes ALL creds)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [H1] Owner rotates workspace credentials → 200 {success, revokedCount}
###      WARNING: this revokes the first-owner bootstrap credential too.
###      Place last so @ownerApiKey is not invalidated mid-suite.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/identity/workspaces/{{bootstrapClaim.response.body.workspaceId}}/credentials/rotate
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{ownerApiKey}}
